course: dictionary
lesson: 7620
title: Probably: a good guess
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Probably» tells you how sure someone is. It means very likely, almost certainly, but not 100% sure. «A shocking post that is on no trusted news site is probably fake.» The writer thinks it is fake, but has not proved it yet.
explain: Look at the words around probably to see why the writer is careful. In «Venus's whole surface is quite young, perhaps 300 to 700 million years old, probably covered over by fresh lava», the clues show a sensible guess based on evidence. A good guess is not the same as a fact.
explain: Probably is not the same as certainly. Try the swap check: if «certainly» fits and the sentence still works, the writer was completely sure. «The Black Death probably started in Central Asia» means historians think this is most likely, but they cannot be completely sure. Check before you say something is true.
fact: Probably means very likely, but not 100% sure.
fact: Words that show chance include likely, unlikely, certain, impossible and probably.
fact: «Most probably» and «probably not» are common phrases in maths and science.
fact: «Lincoln Cathedral in England was probably the tallest building in the world for about 200 years, until its spire fell in 1548.» Probably shows a careful guess about the past.
fact: «The Greenland shark is the longest-living animal with a backbone known, probably at least 270 years.» Probably shows that the age is a well-founded estimate, not an exact number.
exercise: «The shocking post is on no trusted news site, so it is probably fake.» What does probably mean here? | Definitely, with no doubt at all | Impossible, never true | *Very likely, but not certain | Happy and bright
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Lincoln Cathedral was probably the tallest building in the world» that shows a guess. | *probably | world | building | tallest
exercise: Why should you check before saying something is true when someone has written probably? | Because checking makes words longer | Because probably means never | Because probably means it is definitely true | *Because probably is a good guess, not proof
test: «Probably» is an adverb. Which meaning fits it best? | Never, not at all | *Very likely, almost certainly, but not 100% sure | Quickly, in a rush | Certainly, with no doubt at all
test: Which sentence uses probably correctly? | *It is probably going to be sunny, the forecast says so. | Two plus two is probably five, and that is certain. | The dog probably is yesterday. | The moon is probably a sandwich.
exam: Read «The Black Death probably started in Central Asia.» Which word shows the writer is not completely sure? | Death | Central | *probably | Black
